# Interactive Account Navigation

Replace the static profile link in the sidebar with a premium, interactive account menu providing quick access to profile settings, security, and logout.

## Proposed Changes

### Dashboard & Sidebar

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard.html)
- Update `.user-profile-sidebar` to remove the direct `onclick="window.location.href='settings.html'"`.
- Wrap the profile item in a container to manage the relative positioning of the menu.
- Add a hidden `.account-dropdown` menu structure with the following options:
    - **Header**: User name and role (repeated or refined).
    - **Links**: "My Profile", "Settings", "Security", "Support".
    - **Separator**.
    - **Logout**: Move the "Sign Out" button inside this menu.

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard-dark.css](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard-dark.css)
- Style `.account-dropdown`:
    - **Position**: Absolute, bottom: 80px, left: 16px.
    - **Glassmorphism**: Semi-transparent background, heavy blur, subtle border.
    - **Animations**: Slide and fade-in effect when triggered.
    - **Hover States**: Distinct highlights for menu items.
- Style the profile toggle to indicate interactivity (e.g., active state colors).

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard.js)
- Implement toggle logic for the account menu.
- Handle click-outside-to-close behavior.
- Ensure the menu items link correctly to their destinations.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- Click on the profile sidebar item and verify the account menu appears smoothly.
- Test all links within the menu.
- Verify the logout functionality works correctly from its new location.
- Ensure clicking outside the menu closes it.
